{"probes":[{"id":"opnsense-service-contract","summary":"Read-only verification of OPNsense zone addressing, routes, pf/NAT, and direct/published HTTP paths completed.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["configctl interface list returned Action not allowed or missing; equivalent effective state was obtained with ifconfig, netstat, pfctl, and HTTP probes."]},{"id":"opnsense-operational-state","summary":"Read-only operational-state inspection completed on all four nodes.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["configctl firewall list rules returned Action not allowed or missing.","The /var/log/filter.log path was absent; the final node1 command exited 1 after returning its other observations."]}],"assertions":[{"id":"opnsense-zone-addressing","status":"pass","summary":"All declared zone addresses and data-plane routes are present on the intended interfaces; node1's separate management default route does not bypass the zone prefixes.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"ifconfig\nnetstat -rn","observation":"vtnet1/WAN has 10.80.3.1/24, vtnet2/LAN has 10.80.1.1/24, and vtnet3/DMZ has 10.80.2.1/24. Connected routes for 10.80.3.0/24, 10.80.1.0/24, and 10.80.2.0/24 use vtnet1, vtnet2, and vtnet3 respectively; the only default route is the separate management route via 10.100.77.1 on vtnet0."},{"node":"node2","command":"ip -4 addr\nip route\nip route get 10.80.1.10","observation":"10.80.2.10/24 is on enp8s0; default route is via 10.80.2.1 on enp8s0; the LAN destination resolves via 10.80.2.1 dev enp8s0."},{"node":"node3","command":"ip -4 addr\nip route\nip route get 10.80.2.10","observation":"10.80.1.10/24 is on enp8s0; default route is via 10.80.1.1 on enp8s0; the DMZ destination resolves via 10.80.1.1 dev enp8s0."},{"node":"node4","command":"ip -4 addr\nip route\nip route get 10.80.3.1","observation":"10.80.3.10/24 is on enp8s0; default route is via 10.80.3.1 on enp8s0; the WAN gateway is directly reachable on enp8s0."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The supplementary OPNsense interface-view command was unavailable, but the effective interface and routing output was unambiguous."]},{"id":"opnsense-direct-and-published-app","status":"pass","summary":"The DMZ HTTP service returns infraset-dmz directly to LAN and through the single declared WAN 8443 DNAT.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"pfctl -sr 2>&1\npfctl -sn 2>&1","observation":"Active pf contains the LAN rule from vtnet2 to 10.80.2.10 port http-alt and the single relevant rdr: vtnet1 TCP 8443 to 10.80.2.10 port 8080. Saved config contains the WAN TCP port-forward target 10.80.2.10/local-port 8080 with destination port 8443."},{"node":"node2","command":"ss -lntp\ncurl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 5 http://127.0.0.1:8080/","observation":"python3 listens on 0.0.0.0:8080 and the root response contains infraset-dmz."},{"node":"node3","command":"ip route get 10.80.2.10\ncurl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 5 http://10.80.2.10:8080/","observation":"The direct request routes via 10.80.1.1 on enp8s0 and returns infraset-dmz."},{"node":"node4","command":"ip route get 10.80.3.1\ncurl --fail --silent --show-error --max-time 5 http://10.80.3.1:8443/","observation":"The published request reaches 10.80.3.1 directly on enp8s0 and returns infraset-dmz."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"opnsense-state-clean","status":"fail","summary":"Concrete non-history OPNsense configuration backups remain outside the normal /conf/backup history; other inspected services and routes were coherent.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"pfctl -sr 2>&1\npfctl -sn 2>&1\ngrep -nE '<(filter|rule|type|interface|ipprotocol|protocol|descr|source|destination|network|port|nat|outbound|mode|target|local-port|reflection)>' /conf/config.xml 2>&1\nfind /conf -maxdepth 2 -type f -print 2>&1\nfind /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>&1\nps axww | grep -E '[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap' || true\nsockstat -4 -l 2>&1\nconfigctl firewall list rules 2>&1 | head -80","observation":"The saved configuration has /conf/config.xml.[REDACTED] and /conf/config.xml.[REDACTED] alongside, but outside, timestamped /conf/backup files. /tmp also contains debug/old generated files including ifconfig.debug, ifconfig.debug.old, rules.debug.old, vtnet0_oldip, and vtnet0_oldgw. No tcpdump/tshark/dumpcap process was shown. Active pf showed the intended vtnet2 LAN-to-DMZ rule and vtnet1 8443 rdr; no broad WAN transit pass rule was observed."},{"node":"node1","command":"ps axww | grep -E '[c]onfigd|[p]hp-fpm|[l]ighttpd|[u]nbound|[d]nsmasq|[s]shd|[n]tpd'\nstat -f \"%Sm %N\" /conf/config.xml /conf/event_config_changed.json /tmp/rules.debug /tmp/rules.debug.old 2>&1\nfind /conf -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>&1\nfind /conf/backup -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>&1\ntail -20 /var/log/filter.log 2>&1","observation":"Core OPNsense processes were present; the non-history config backups were confirmed separately from normal backup history. Generated rules.debug and rules.debug.old exist. The filter log path does not exist, causing exit code 1."},{"node":"node2","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain\nip route show table main\nss -lntup\nsystemctl is-enabled ssh.service 2>&1\nsystemctl is-active ssh.service 2>&1\nps -eo pid,user,comm,args | grep -E '[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap' || true\nfind /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>&1","observation":"No failed units, capture process, or temp-file residue was shown. Routes contain the intended DMZ default gateway; listeners are resolver, SSH socket activation, and the intended HTTP service on 8080. ssh.service reports disabled and inactive."},{"node":"node3","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain\nip route show table main\nss -lntup\nsystemctl is-enabled ssh.service 2>&1\nsystemctl is-active ssh.service 2>&1\nps -eo pid,user,comm,args | grep -E '[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap' || true\nfind /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>&1","observation":"No failed units, capture process, or temp-file residue was shown. Routes contain the intended LAN default gateway; only resolver and SSH socket listeners are present. ssh.service reports disabled and inactive."},{"node":"node4","command":"systemctl --failed --no-legend --plain\nip route show table main\nss -lntup\nsystemctl is-enabled ssh.service 2>&1\nsystemctl is-active ssh.service 2>&1\nps -eo pid,user,comm,args | grep -E '[t]cpdump|[t]shark|[d]umpcap' || true\nfind /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 1 -type f -print 2>&1","observation":"No failed units, capture process, or temp-file residue was shown. Routes contain the intended WAN default gateway; only resolver and SSH socket listeners are present. ssh.service reports disabled and inactive."}],"failures":["Non-history files /conf/config.xml.[REDACTED] and /conf/config.xml.[REDACTED] remain outside the normal /conf/backup history."],"limitations":["The missing filter.log prevents a complete log-state decision.","The unavailable configctl firewall-list action limits that view to the successful pfctl and saved-config evidence."]}],"actions_performed":["Executed four read-only managed exec calls for Probe 1 and five read-only managed exec calls for Probe 2, within their respective budgets.","Performed no mutations, controlled failures, reboots, or evaluator cleanup because both authored probes were read-only.","Called complete_evidence exactly once after all live checks completed."],"overall_summary":"Zone addressing and both required application paths pass. Operational-state cleanliness fails because non-history OPNsense configuration backups remain; live evidence is closed."}
